  abstract={Pathlines of fluid flow are strategically guided through additively manufactured ceramic structures with specified porosity and pore diameter variations. With additional tunable parameters such as printing layer thickness and ceramic particle size, tailored porous structures hold opportunities for application-specific designs in thermofluidic systems. Further details can be found in the article number 2000158 by Sadaf Sobhani and co-workers.},
